<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  com.claude.pane-close-drainer — row 4. Every 5 min: retry the queued pane closes.

  WHY ITS OWN JOB (measured 2026-10-23, docs/plans/pane-end-of-life-2026-10-22.md item C5). The
  drainer (scripts/pane-close-retry.sh) used to ride com.claude.teammate-reap-alarm, which is
  ProcessType Background, Nice 10, LowPriorityIO, every 600 s. At load ~150 that job got almost no
  CPU: one run held its launchd slot for 75+ minutes inside assignee-pane-residency.sh, the drainer
  started 7 minutes into the run and was cut at its 240 s budget, and the last queued pane never got
  a turn. launchd starts no new run of a job that is still executing, so a starved alarm starved the
  drainer with it. A pane close is on the operator's latency path, so this job is ProcessType
  Standard with NO Nice and NO LowPriorityIO (operator ruling: latency-path daemons get no Nice).

  WHY A 5-MIN CADENCE COSTS ALMOST NOTHING: with no rows queued the drainer exits before it asks
  kitty anything. It takes a single-instance lock, so an overlapping tick is a no-op.

  BOUNDS. CC_PCQ_DRAIN_TIMEOUT_S=240 is the drainer's own run budget; the outer
  `timeout -k 5 270` is the backstop if that budget itself wedges, still inside the 300 s interval.
  The timeout path is absolute because a bare Homebrew name does not exist under a launchd PATH.

  PATH prepends ~/.claude/bin AND /opt/homebrew/bin via bash -c so $HOME expands at runtime: the
  drainer needs kitty/it2 (~/.claude/bin) and jq (Homebrew).

  RunAtLoad false — a login must not fire a kitty probe. Activated by install.sh on converge
  (declared `run` in launchd/fleet.manifest).
  Kill switch after load: launchctl bootout gui/$UID/com.claude.pane-close-drainer.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.claude.pane-close-drainer</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>-c</string>
        <string>export PATH="$HOME/.claude/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin"; export CC_PCQ_DRAIN_TIMEOUT_S=240; exec /opt/homebrew/bin/timeout -k 5 270 /bin/bash "$HOME/.claude/scripts/pane-close-retry.sh"</string>
    </array>

    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>300</integer>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>

    <key>ProcessType</key>      <string>Standard</string>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>  <string>/Users/chrisren/.claude/logs/pane-close-drainer.out.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>/Users/chrisren/.claude/logs/pane-close-drainer.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
